[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2999377447","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/2152#issuecomment-2999377447","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/2152","id":2999377447,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6yxt4n","user":{"login":"mj12albert","id":4997971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTc5NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4997971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert","html_url":"https://github.com/mj12albert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-24T08:41:43Z","updated_at":"2025-06-24T08:41:43Z","body":"> I can't seem to find a way to let the input accept special characters.\n\nGenerally event handlers have a `preventBaseUIHandler` method that you can call to skip the component's internal logic and override it with your own:\n```jsx\n<NumberField.Input\n  onKeyDown={(event) => {\n    event.preventBaseUIHandler();\n    // your logic instead\n  }}\n/>\n```\nHowever for this case I'm not sure if this is possible because it may skip so much that it could affect other features\n\n> Can Number Field be used to evaluate equations?\n\nThis isn't really a use-case we considered for Numberfield 😅 are you making something like a spreadsheet app? @woodward54 ","author_association":"MEMB